* mmbt5551.lib - Diodes Incorporated MMBT5551, high-voltage NPN, SOT-23.
* VENDOR MODEL, COPIED VERBATIM FROM THE MANUFACTURER'S OWN FILE.
*
* USAGE:
*   .include models/bjt_npn/mmbt5551.lib
*   Q1 collector base emitter MMBT5551
*
* Role in this project: FIVE instances per gain block - the tail current
* sink (circuits/preamp/gain_block.py:262), the two ADR-014 cascodes
* (291-292), the VAS load (328) and the Vbe multiplier (350). It is the
* most-instantiated active device in the design, which is why its beta
* spread matters: the datasheet window is 80..250 and whether the two
* cascodes tolerate that spread is a Fase 4 question of the same family
* as NC-013.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* THE PART THE PROJECT BUYS IS THE MMBT5551, NOT THE 2N5551
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* Same die, SOT-23 instead of TO-92 - see the header of
* models/bjt_pnp/mmbt5401.lib, its PNP complement, for the full
* reasoning and what the package change costs (ADR-017). One consequence
* is specific to this device: the Vbe multiplier at gain_block.py:350
* carries an explicit placement rule - "MUST be thermally coupled to the
* NPN output device's tab (thermal compound + cable tie)" - and A SOT-23
* CANNOT BE CABLE-TIED TO A TO-220 TAB. That is NC-019, to be resolved
* before G2.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* PROVENANCE - the short version. Full record in
* models/bjt_npn/mmbt5551.provenance.json, the freeze in
* vendor/bjt_npn/diodes_inc/MMBT5551/PROVENANCE.json, and the reasoning
* in docs/preamp/reports/2026-09-10-L24-t7-dispositivi-attivi.md
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* Diodes serves this model as a text file, so it was frozen byte-for-byte
* at vendor/bjt_npn/diodes_inc/MMBT5551/MMBT5551.spice.txt and copied
* here unchanged. NOTHING WAS REMOVED - there is no mfg= to strip, unlike
* the two Linear Systems models. No value was rounded, reordered or
* "corrected"; note in particular that the vendor writes "RB =0.26" and
* "RE =0.23" with a space before the equals sign, and THAT SPACE IS KEPT.
* ngspice parses it without complaint. The vendor's AS-IS warranty
* disclaimer is reproduced below unaltered.
*
* Checkable, not asserted:
*
*   diff <(grep -v '^\*' vendor/bjt_npn/diodes_inc/MMBT5551/MMBT5551.spice.txt) \
*        <(grep -v '^\*' models/bjt_npn/mmbt5551.lib)      # empty
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* PSPICE QUASI-SATURATION PARAMETERS: ngspice ACCEPTS THEM SILENTLY
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* QUASIMOD=1, RCO=170, VO=35 and GAMMA=2.2E-7 are PSpice quasi-saturation
* parameters and ngspice 47 emits ZERO warnings on this file - verified
* by running it in L25. The silence is evidence only because the
* comparison exists: on models/jfet/lsk489.lib the same ngspice prints
* four "unrecognized parameter ... ignored" lines.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* CROSS-CHECKED AGAINST THE DATASHEET - THREE OF THREE INSIDE
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* Datasheet DS30061 Rev. 15-2 (c) 2025, revision read from the footer,
* frozen at vendor/bjt_npn/diodes_inc/MMBT5551/MMBT5551.pdf. ngspice 47,
* set temp = 25 (the datasheet is @ 25 C, ngspice defaults to 27, and
* XTB = 1.4 makes hFE temperature dependent):
*
*   hFE   @ IC = 10 mA, VCE = 5 V      107.218    window 80 .. 250   INSIDE
*   fT    @ IC = 10 mA, VCE = 10 V,
*         ftest = 100 MHz              175.683 MHz   100 MHz MIN.    INSIDE
*   C_obo @ VCB = 10 V, 1 MHz          2.2207 pF     6 pF MAX.       INSIDE
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* TWO NOTES ON THE fT NUMBER
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* FIRST: it was measured with the collector current VERIFIED at the
* datasheet's IC = 10.000 mA (op prints 1.000000e-02), not at a round
* base current - which is what moved the MMBT5401's figure by 5.5%; see
* that file's header. L24 records 173.1 MHz for this device.
*
* SECOND, and this is a property of the model rather than of the method:
* on this device THE DEFINITION MATTERS, where on the MMBT5401 it did
* not. The datasheet specifies fT as the gain-bandwidth product measured
* at ftest = 100 MHz, and that gives 175.683 MHz - the value locked here,
* because it is what the 100 MHz minimum refers to. The |hfe| = 1
* crossing gives 172.579 MHz instead, 1.8% lower, because the roll-off is
* not a clean -20 dB/dec all the way to unity: GBW peaks at 176.9 MHz
* near 30 MHz and then falls, reaching 105 MHz by 1 GHz. Anyone quoting
* an fT for this device should say which definition they used.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* WHAT THIS MODEL DOES NOT HAVE
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* NO FLICKER NOISE FROM THE MANUFACTURER: the vendor line has no KF, no
* AF. Until L44 every noise figure that leaned on this device was a floor
* without flicker (NC-004). Since L44 (ADR-057) a declared upper bound,
* KF = 1e-13 AF = 1.4, is appended at the END of this file, outside the
* vendor block - read the L44 section there before quoting a noise figure.
*
* No SPICE magnitude suffix appears in the model line, so
* docs/limitations.md #13 has nothing to bite on here.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* BELOW THIS LINE: THE VENDOR FILE, BYTE FOR BYTE
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* DIODES INCORPORATED AND ITS AFFILIATED COMPANIES AND SUBSIDIARIES (COLLECTIVELY, "DIODES") 
* PROVIDE THESE SPICE MODELS AND DATA (COLLECTIVELY, THE "SM DATA") "AS IS" AND WITHOUT ANY 
* REPRESENTATIONS OR WARRANTIES, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING ANY WARRANTY OF MERCHANTABILITY 
* OR FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, ANY WARRANTY ARISING FROM COURSE OF DEALING OR COURSE OF 
* PERFORMANCE, OR ANY WARRANTY THAT ACCESS TO OR OPERATION OF THE SM DATA WILL BE UNINTERRUPTED, 
* OR THAT THE SM DATA OR ANY SIMULATION USING THE SM DATA WILL BE ERROR FREE. TO THE MAXIMUM 
* EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, IN NO EVENT WILL DIODES BE LIABLE FOR ANY DIRECT OR INDIRECT, 
* SPECIAL, INCIDENTAL, PUNITIVE OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES ARISING OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH 
* THE PRODUCTION OR USE OF SM DATA, HOWEVER CAUSED AND UNDER WHATEVER CAUSE OF ACTION OR THEORY 
* OF LIABILITY BROUGHT (INCLUDING, WITHOUT LIMITATION, UNDER ANY CONTRACT, NEGLIGENCE OR OTHER 
* TORT THEORY OF LIABILITY), EVEN IF DIODES HAS BEEN ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES, 
* AND DIODES' TOTAL LIABILITY (WHETHER IN CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE) WITH REGARD TO THE SM 
* DATA WILL NOT, IN THE AGGREGATE, EXCEED ANY SUMS PAID BY YOU TO DIODES FOR THE SM DATA.



*
*DIODES_INC_SPICE_MODEL
*ORIGIN=DZSL_DPG_GM
*SIMULATOR=PSPICE
*DATE=08FEB2011
*VERSION=2
*
.MODEL MMBT5551 NPN IS=6.5E-15 NF=1 BF=110 VAF=288 ISE=1.0E-14
+ NE=1.5 NR=1 BR=4.5 VAR=70 ISC=3E-12 NC=1.35 RC=0.5 RB =0.26 RE =0.23
+ CJC=6.1E-12 MJC=0.31 VJC=0.4 CJE=57E-12 MJE=0.35 VJE=0.8 TF=0.2E-9
+ TR=1.5E-6 XTB=1.4 QUASIMOD=1 RCO=170 VO=35 GAMMA=2.2E-7
*
*$
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* L44 (ADR-057): FLICKER NOISE ADDED - NOT FROM THE MANUFACTURER
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* The '+' line at the very end CONTINUES the .MODEL card above: ngspice
* joins it to the last card and skips the comment lines in between, and
* when a parameter repeats the LAST value wins. Measured in L44, not
* assumed, and re-measured on every run by the [flicker] check in
* scripts/validate_models.py (base-current noise, KF read back from
* S(10 Hz) - S(10 kHz)). It sits OUTSIDE the vendor block so that the
* vendor bytes stay exactly as served: the non-comment diff against the
* file under vendor/ is this one line and nothing else.
*
* WHAT THE NUMBERS ARE. ngspice: i_n^2 = 2 q Ib + KF Ib^AF / f. KF = 1e-13
* with AF = 1.4 is a DECLARED UPPER BOUND for the small-signal bipolar
* class, not a fit to this part. Sources (PDFs and readings under vendor/,
* PROVENANCE files next to them):
*   - 2N5087, Motorola, Fig. 2 p. 3 (vendor/bjt_pnp/motorola/2N5087/):
*     AF = 1.35 consistent over 10 uA..1 mA, KF ~2e-14 at 10 Hz, ~5e-14
*     at 300 Hz;
*   - Linear Systems databook, "Solving the Noise Puzzle", Fig. 3 p. 329
*     (LS310/LS350 family): AF ~1.46, KF ~6e-14; worst case ~2x typical.
*   Typical class value 5e-14; the bound is 2x that.
*
* FOR THIS PART THERE IS NO CURVE: the L44 search found none for the
* 2N5551/MMBT5551 (NXP, Fairchild, Motorola sheets give a single NF
* figure). The NPN gets the PNP-class bound by DECLARED CHOICE; the
* nearest NPN curve found (2N5089, a very-high-gain type) is weaker
* evidence and was not used for a number.
* What it buys: E5 with this bound on every bipolar device is 5.53 uV
* worst case against 9.95 (5.1 dB margin); a bound 10x higher still gives
* 8.57 uV. data/2026-10-01/L44/, report 2026-10-01-L44-rumore-1f.md.
+ KF=1e-13 AF=1.4
